  "[silence] (to O-lan) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "O-lan (to Wang Lung): \"Why do you say that? I am not a pig. I eat my fill and I give you your fill. I am not a beggar. I have given you all I have---\"",
  "[says] O-lan recalls the pearls she kept.",
  "O-lan (to Wang Lung): \"I have given you all I have, and I have yet to give you the children---\"",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"They are not all mine, they are not all mine,\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung covers face.",
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) O-lan expresses disappointment.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"Now, and you may go back to the kitchen of the Great House---\"",
  "[says] Wang Lung expresses regret about O-lan's past.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"But I did not mean to say that you were not mine, I only meant that those two are not mine, they are not mine. You have given me the land, I have the land. What else can a man need?\"",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"Here is the land, it is my own now, and I have jewels and gold hidden away. What more can I need?\"",
